  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mitigating climate change: Towards circular cities in the Netherlands and China</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pilot cities have been chosen in the Guangdong Province, where circularity is being promoted and a province-wide zero-waste city strategy is being planned. In 2035 the goal is to reach full coverage for all cities.To foster the interaction on circular cities between the Netherlands and China to mitigate climate change, the programme focusses on developments in both countries. It aims to connect the Dutch and Chinese triple helix for knowledge exchange and identify areas for collaboration.In the long term, the purpose is to facilitate structural policy dialogues that support Dutch policy making, as well as multi-annual knowledge and trade partnerships that contribute to the Dutch earning capacity.</narrative>
  </description>
